        "activation_committed_questions": 0,
        "original_system": "Analyze a completed PAST trajectory (feedback already released) using its released released label/reward and actual images/observations.\nIdentify a transferable turning point, not a diagnosis lookup or current answer. Attribute each injected skill:\nADOPTED_POSITIVE, ADOPTED_NEGATIVE, or IGNORED. For adoption cite a zero-based step_index and concise evidence\nof changed action/interpretation; mere presence in context is not adoption. Attribution is provisional, not causal proof.\nReturn JSON: {\"skill_adoption\":[{\"skill_id\":\"...\",\"status\":\"...\",\"step_index\":0,\"evidence\":\"...\"}],\n\"extracted_pattern\":\"...\",\"output_intent\":\"CREATE|PATCH|NONE\",\"patch_target_id\":null,\n\"branch\":\"general|task_level|action_level\"}.\nGeneral = concrete domain-agnostic process; task_level = clinical task/tool choice or sequence;\naction_level = one tool's input/output operation. NONE for unsupported, case-specific or trivial lessons.\nDo not infer a specific lesion solely from a binary source answer. State uncertainty. Never assume unexecuted tools ran.\n",
        "clarification": "\n\nEXPLICIT ATTRIBUTION UNIQUENESS CONTRACT; no new clinical information or source evidence.\nReport each injected skill_id at most once in skill_adoption. A single entry must represent that skill's adoption in this trajectory using the one best supported actual zero-based step_index and its concise evidence; do not create separate entries for multiple steps.\nKeep the original ADOPTED_POSITIVE, ADOPTED_NEGATIVE and IGNORED meanings, original source-evidence requirements and all other output fields unchanged. Never invent an injected ID, step, tool execution or patient fact. This is a uniqueness/schema clarification, not a new clinical guideline.\n",
        "ordinary_event_rule": "system == original ANALYZE and event == 'analysis_' + payload['trajectory']['id']",
